  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we split the whole into $3$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/37d524644c009517608455822101750eb532cc8858fee1b96516d30e3fa1fe15.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{2}{12}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{12}.\n$$",
